  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "Provider paging tokens must remain bounded serializable scalar metadata at observation, journal identity, persisted acknowledgement and later inspection boundaries; malformed progress cannot adopt ownership, charge usage or settle work.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/execution_io.mjs",
        "lib/execution_journal.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/config.mjs",
        "test/execution-backends.test.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "Inspection and acceptance lookup share assertExecutionCursor before journaling or progress/identity/cost adoption. The fixed exported limit is 4096 serialized UTF-8 JSON bytes, including quotes and escapes.",
        "Null/omitted tokens retain the existing cursor. Strings, finite numbers and booleans remain valid bounded scalars; objects, arrays, cycles, BigInt, functions, symbols, nonfinite numbers and oversized strings are rejected without invoking custom toJSON.",
        "Reconciliation rejects malformed terminal observations as scoped EXECUTION_PROTOCOL backoff while preserving previous cursor, observation time, acceptance, ownership, cost and journal bytes. No independent read-only polling or replacement paid dispatch occurs.",
        "Subsequent inspection sends only a previously validated token. Lost-acknowledgement lookup remains unresolved until a valid owned observation reconciles the original key; no second submit is issued.",
        "The current cursor and every recorded acknowledgement cursor are validated on remote state reads before transport calls or rewrites. Invalid pre-upgrade state is preserved with an explicit exact-checkpoint recovery remedy; resetting tokens, deleting intents or redispatching is not a migration.",
        "Long valid cursor gap identities use the existing digest helper only when the legacy gap ID exceeds the journal 512-character bound. Hashed IDs use the distinct gap: prefix so short digest lookalike tokens cannot suppress a different gap. Short IDs remain unchanged; restart replay retains stable event IDs and ordered sequences without duplicate appends.",
        "Execution and job projections remain bounded by the cursor contract; no event-page, log-retention, provider-availability, model/provider-default, credential, policy or human-merge boundary is relaxed."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "inspection and acceptance lookup reject invalid cursors before journaling or adopting progress",
        "bounded JSON scalar cursors survive restart and long-cursor gap replay without growing identities",
        "invalid persisted cursors refuse inspection and redispatch with a checkpoint recovery remedy",
        "missing results remain retrieving, event gaps are explicit and recovered events deduplicate"
      ]
    }
  ],
